1
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:27,600
One morning, you see a number above your head.

2
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:35,400
17,412. Days left.

3
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:44,400
Everyone has one.

4
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:49,600
Some are big.

5
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:54,600
Some are not.

6
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:02,400
"17,000 days. Plenty of time."

7
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:10,400
So you spend them like you always did.

8
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:17,600
Mom calls. "Later."

9
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:24,600
Then one Sunday, you finally went home.

10
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:31,400
She was so happy to see you.

11
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:37,600
And then you saw her number.

12
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:41,600
214.

13
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,600
That's 30 Sundays.

14
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:55,400
30 Sunday dinners. If you come.

15
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:03,400
You had thousands of days.

16
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:08,400
She had 214.

17
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:12,600
So you changed everything.

18
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:20,400
Every Sunday at her table.

19
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:28,400
She taught you her recipes.

20
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,400
You asked about her life.

21
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:43,400
On the days you couldn't come, you called.

22
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:51,400
You stopped counting your days.

23
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:59,400
You started making them count.

24
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:12,400
And when her number reached zero...

25
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:25,400
...you had no regrets.

26
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:31,600
Only memories.

27
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:37,600
You can't see your number.

28
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:43,400
But it's counting.

29
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:49,400
Everyone you love has a number.

30
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:55,400
Don't wait to see it.

31
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:02,200
Call them today.

